{
  // PROVIDER ALIGNMENT (2026-10-24, Drew): both machines carry the same
  // providers; unneeded ones are disabled here, identically on both.
  // - Token-based Google/Gemini paths are OFF. EARMARK: when a token-based
  //   Gemini path is wanted one day, use the "google" provider below — it is
  //   THE token path (Gemini API key; working muse-sandbox free-tier key is
  //   in the credential store as "Google API (muse-sandbox)").
  // - THE Antigravity provider is "antigravity-ls" (warm language-server
  //   route). "antigravity-agy" (CLI spawn route) sat disabled as the
  //   fallback until 2026-10-28, when Drew re-enabled it for one seated
  //   purpose: the agy CLI is a door that serves Gemini 4 Argon, so
  //   argon-plan seats antigravity-agy/gemini-4-argon. Its other models
  //   stay route-gated (seated nowhere).
  // - 2026-10-30 (Drew): the Antigravity doors consolidated on
  //   "antigravity-direct" — a proxy that speaks the agy CLI's own wire
  //   protocol directly (keyring OAuth credential, the CLI's refresh
  //   client, its v1internal envelope to daily-cloudcode-pa) with no
  //   spawned CLI and no spawned language server. "antigravity-ls" and
  //   "antigravity-agy" are in disabled_providers below and their proxy
  //   services are retired in home/common/default.nix; their definitions
  //   stay FULL below per the switchboard rule. The Gemini seats moved
  //   to antigravity-direct (gemini-flash-plan, argon-plan). The Claude
  //   seats in sonnet-plan and opus-plan still name antigravity-ls:
  //   they are inert while the provider is disabled, until they are
  //   re-pointed or the door is restored. Undo: delete both ids from
  //   disabled_providers, restore the two proxy units, re-point seats.
  //   2026-10-30 (Drew, later the same day): "only the direct —
  //   replace all others": the sonnet-plan and opus-plan Claude seats
  //   are re-pointed to antigravity-direct as well; no route leaf
  //   names antigravity-ls or antigravity-agy anymore.
  // - "claude-code" is TEMPORARILY disabled (2026-10-27, Drew): the Claude
  //   plan is on the FREE tier for now and the API may be down. The setup
  //   itself is confirmed working — the proxy (:18749) is live and serves
  //   claude-haiku-5-5 (verified 2026-10-27) — this is a config-level pause
  //   only: the proxy, its catalog entries, and every route that references
  //   it stay in place. Claude MODELS via other plans (antigravity-ls,
  //   cline-pass, opendesign leaves in haiku/sonnet/opus-plan) are NOT the
  //   Claude plan and are unaffected. To re-enable: delete "claude-code"
  //   from disabled_providers and restore the "default" below.
  // To re-enable a provider: delete its id from disabled_providers.
  // That list is the PROVIDER SWITCHBOARD — see the comment block directly
  // above it for the full mechanism.
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "autoupdate": true,
  // ==========================================================================
  // PROVIDER SWITCHBOARD — the ONE place providers are turned on and off.
  //
  // A provider is ON unless its id appears in disabled_providers below.
  // To turn a provider OFF: add its id to the list. To turn it back ON:
  // delete its id from the list. That one-line edit is the whole job —
  // nothing else in this file needs to change.
  //
  // Every fleet provider keeps its FULL definition (models, options) in the
  // "provider" block below at all times, disabled or not, so re-enabling
  // never requires reconstructing config. The only step beyond the flip is
  // the provider's own sign-in / credential, which lives outside this file.
  //
  // Providers with NO definition below (google-vertex, nvidia, vercel,
  // huggingface, opencode, github-copilot) are opencode built-ins: the app
  // ships their catalogs, so the list alone switches them — no definition
  // is missing.
  //
  // Route pools need no edits either: a pool leaf pointing at an OFF
  // provider simply yields nothing until that provider is flipped back on
  // (the pools below already ship that way — haiku-plan seats claude-code
  // while it is off).
  //
  // WORKED EXAMPLE — Claude: "claude-code" sits in the list today because
  // the Claude plan is on the free tier (see the header note). The day it
  // comes back, delete the "claude-code" line from the list and Claude is
  // live: its definition, model catalog, and haiku-plan seat are already in
  // place, and every tier that consumes haiku-plan (scout, workhorse,
  // speed, luna-haiku-100k) picks it up on its own. The only remaining step
  // is the claude.ai sign-in. (Restoring "default" to
  // claude-code/claude-haiku-5-5 is an optional preference, NOT part of
  // enabling — the workhorse default works either way.)
  //
  // REVERSED 2026-10-30 (Drew, direct order): "muse" leaves this list.
  // The direct "meta" door is dead by Meta's design (attestation —
  // see the note at the "muse" provider), so muse-proxy is now the
  // only working door into the same single Meta pool, and the
  // routes seat muse/* leaves where the meta/* leaves sat, at the
  // same weights and positions.
  //
  // KNOWN EXCEPTION: the design-code / code-design / open-design proxy
  // blocks further down stay commented out (preserved legacy: four blocks,
  // three ids, two keyed "design-code"). They are off via this list too,
  // but re-enabling one needs a dedupe decision first. Their live door is
  // "opendesign" (on).
  // ==========================================================================
  // 2026-10-30 (route audit): "deepseek" joins the list below. Its
  // definition is the DeepSeek OFFICIAL API — a pay-as-you-go funds
  // door, not a plan pool — and no route seats it (DeepSeek models
  // reach the tiers through the plan doors: OpenCode Go, ClinePass,
  // OpenDesign, Command Code). It has taken no traffic since
  // 2026-10-25. Per the switchboard rule this flip is the whole job;
  // its full definition stays in the provider block, and deleting
  // the line re-enables it if the direct door is ever wanted.
  // 2026-10-30 (Drew, direct order): "meta" joins the list below.
  // The direct api.meta.ai door is dead by Meta's design — the plan
  // API key returns 403 client_attestation_denied from any
  // non-Muse-Code client and the OAuth token 401s (see the note at
  // the "muse" provider). The routes no longer seat meta/* leaves
  // (#2635 moved them to muse/* via muse-proxy, the working door).
  // Per the switchboard rule the full definition stays in the
  // provider block; deleting this line re-enables it if Meta ever
  // serves this client again.
  // 2026-10-30 (Drew, direct order — supersedes the two notes above):
  // "muse" joins the list too, and "muse-direct" replaces BOTH older
  // Meta doors. muse-proxy's direct mode (#2753) exchanges the Muse
  // CLI account token for the plan's minted key and speaks the
  // Responses API — the route that accepts that key — so the fleet no
  // longer needs the CLI-harness door ("muse") or the attestation-dead
  // direct door ("meta"). muse-direct is the ONLY enabled Meta-family
  // provider; both older definitions stay FULL below per the
  // switchboard rule, and the routes' Meta leaves were retargeted to
  // muse-direct contributor models in the same pass.
  // 2026-10-31 (Drew, direct order): "commandcode" joins the list.
  // Its credits are exhausted (about ten cents left, expired the morning
  // of 2026-10-31) and an empty pool must not run: sessions were
  // still being routed onto its leaves (deepseek-flash-plan,
  // spark-plan, sol-plan, beam-plan, mimo-flash-plan, scout) and
  // retry-looping on "insufficient credits". Per the switchboard
  // rule the definition and every seat stay in place; deleting
  // this line re-enables Command Code if it is ever refilled.
  "disabled_providers": [
    "google",
    "google-vertex",
    "cloudflare-ai-gateway",
    "groq",
    "nvidia",
    "vercel",
    "huggingface",
    "opencode",
    "github-copilot",
    "openai-codex",
    "chatgpt",
    "openrouter",
    "cloudflare-gateway",
    "cloudflare-workers-ai",
    "code-design",
    "design-code",
    "open-design",
    "deepseek",
    "claude-code",
    "meta",
    "muse",
    "antigravity-ls",
    "antigravity-agy",
    "commandcode"
  ],
  // Default was "claude-code/claude-haiku-5-5" until the 2026-10-27 Claude
  // pause (see the header note). Workhorse is the fleet's standard tier and
  // what agent configs already default to; restoring the Haiku default
  // when claude-code is re-enabled is an optional preference, not part of
  // enabling it (see the PROVIDER SWITCHBOARD above).
  // claude-code is re-enabled.
  "default": "opencode-route/workhorse",
  // The v2 default-model key is "model" (config normalize.ts reads only
  // input.model; the "default" key above is not consumed by the 2.x schema
  // and the server otherwise falls back to its first-available model —
  // which was commandcode/gpt-5.6-terra, failing over to gpt-6-luna.
  // Verified 2026-10-29 against /api/model/default. Drew’s ruling: a
  // session with no model chosen resolves to the workhorse route.
  "model": "opencode-route/workhorse",
  // Small-model slot (2026-10-29, Drew): the route `speed`, never a direct
  // provider leaf. OpenChamber’s small-model resolver reads this key (or
  // the title agent’s model) when no settings override applies; a capable
  // route is deliberate — compaction and summaries have to read a lot, so
  // the slot is a real tier, not the cheapest model on any plan.
  "small_model": "opencode-route/speed",
  // Messaging embeddings OFF (2026-10-29, Drew): the messaging.embedding
  // tier defaults to a local Qwen3-Embedding llama-server that autostarts
  // with every OpenCode process (standing server + OpenChamber managed
  // instance). Tier off disables it; semantic message search degrades to
  // the fuzzy FTS fallback. Re-enable by removing this key.
  "messaging": {
    "embedding": "off"
  },
  "provider": {
    "claude-code": {
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
      "name": "Claude Code (CLI proxy)",
      "options": {
        "baseURL": "http://127.0.0.1:{env:CLAUDE_CODE_PROXY_PORT:-18749}/v1",
        "apiKey": "claude-code-local"
      },
      "models": {
        "claude-haiku-5-5": {
          "name": "Haiku 5.5 (Claude Code)",
          "variants": {
            "low": {
              "options": {
                "thinking": {
                  "type": "enabled",
                  "budget_tokens": 4096
                }
              }
            },
            "medium": {
              "options": {
                "thinking": {
                  "type": "enabled",
                  "budget_tokens": 8192
                }
              }
            },
            "high": {
